# GeT-RM reference material, Coriell ID HG00599 (Han Chinese South, China,
# 1000 Genomes). GeT-RM consensus diplotype: *2/*2 (4/4 labs tested
# agreeing). Source: Pratt VM et al., "Characterization of Reference
# Materials for TPMT and NUDT15: A GeT-RM Collaborative Project." J Mol
# Diagn 2022;24:1079-1088 (PMID 35850928), Table 2, as reproduced in CDC's
# public-domain data table
# (https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/media/pdfs/2024/08/TPMT-and-NUDT15-reference-materials_508C.pdf,
# retrieved 2026-08-19). Genotype below constructed from this project's own
# dbSNP-confirmed defining-variant coordinate (genes/nudt15.py), not
# redistributed from GeT-RM/Coriell/CDC directly.
#
# Nomenclature note: the 2022 paper used pre-2025-consolidation NUDT15
# nomenclature, where *2 = R139C + the GAGTCG insertion in cis. PharmVar's
# 2025 update folded *2 into *3 (as suballele *3.002); this project's
# single-locus scope (R139C only, see genes/nudt15.py) cannot distinguish
# *3.002 from plain *3 (*3.001) either way -- both are homozygous R139C
# here, so this sample presents as *3/*3 to this module. The FUNCTIONAL
# call (Poor Metabolizer, two no-function alleles) is unaffected by that
# suballele-identity gap; see docs/VALIDATION.md.
#CHROM	POS	ID	REF	ALT	QUAL	FILTER	INFO	FORMAT	SAMPLE1
chr13	48045719	rs116855232	C	T	99	PASS	.	GT	1/1
